# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep two things out of image layers:
#
#   .env     the shared token. An image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image,
#            and `docker history` survives deleting the file in a later layer.
#   output/  rendered documents. These contain PHI and are meant to be transient - in the
#            deployment they live on a tmpfs precisely so they never touch a disk.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs `app/` and `templates/`, so nothing here is required for the
# build to work; this is defence in depth against a future COPY . .

.env
.env.*
output/
samples/

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

tests/
scripts/make_samples.py

*.log
*.tmp
